Inspection ID: RedundantRequireNotNullCall

fullDescription.text:
Reports properties that do not follow the naming conventions. The following properties are reported: Top-level properties Properties in objects and companion objects You can specify the required pattern in the inspection options. Recommended naming conventions: it has to start with an uppercase letter, use camel case and no underscores. Example: '// top-level property
  val USER_NAME_FIELD = "UserName"
  // top-level property holding reference to singleton object
  val PersonComparator: Comparator<Person> = /*...*/

  class Person {
    companion object {
      // property in companion object
      val NO_NAME = Person()
    }
  }' Inspection ID: ObjectPropertyName

fullDescription.markdown:
Reports properties that do not follow the naming conventions.

The following properties are reported:

* Top-level properties
* Properties in objects and companion objects

You can specify the required pattern in the inspection options.

[Recommended naming conventions](https://kotlinlang.org/docs/coding-conventions.html#naming-rules): it has to start with an uppercase letter, use camel case and no underscores.

**Example:**


      // top-level property
      val USER_NAME_FIELD = "UserName"
      // top-level property holding reference to singleton object
      val PersonComparator: Comparator<Person> = /*...*/

      class Person {
        companion object {
          // property in companion object
          val NO_NAME = Person()
        }
      }

Inspection ID: ObjectPropertyName

