Reports 'runBlocking' calls inside 'suspend' functions. Using 'runBlocking' within a 'suspend' function blocks the calling thread and defeats the purpose of asynchronous programming. The quick-fix replaces the 'runBlocking' call with one of the following alternatives, depending on the context: A 'run' call. A 'withContext' call when a specific 'CoroutineContext' is used. Directly inlined code without the 'runBlocking' wrapper. Example: 'suspend fun something() {
  runBlocking {
    code() // The thread is blocked here
  }
}' After the quick-fix is applied: 'suspend fun something() {
  code() // Runs asynchronously
}' Inspection ID: RunBlockingInSuspendFunction New in 2025.1

fullDescription.markdown:
