fullDescription.text:
Reports any references to local non-'Serializable' variables outside 'Serializable' lambdas, local and anonymous classes. When a local variable is referenced from an anonymous class, its value is stored in an implicit field of that class. The same happens for local classes and lambdas. If the variable is of a non-'Serializable' type, serialization will fail. Example: 'interface A extends Serializable {
      abstract void foo();
  }
  class B {}
  class C {
      void foo() {
          B b = new B();
          A a = new A() {
              @Override
              public void foo() {
                  System.out.println(b); // warning
              }
          };
      }
  }' Inspection ID: SerializableStoresNonSerializable

