Reports calls to 'java.sql.Statement.execute()' or any of its variants which take a dynamically-constructed string as the query to execute. Constructed SQL statements are a common source of security breaches. By default, this inspection ignores compile-time constants. Example: 'ResultSet execute(Statement statement, String name) throws SQLException {
