     */
    @Deprecated
    public void oldAndBusted() {}

    public void newHotness() {}
  }
  class ElseWhere {
    void x(Interesting i) {
      i.oldAndBusted(); // deprecated warning here
    }
  }' After the quick-fix is applied: 'class Interesting {

    /**
     * @deprecated Use {@link #newHotness()} instead
     */
    @Deprecated
    public void oldAndBusted() {}

    public void newHotness() {}
  }
  class ElseWhere {
    void x(Interesting i) {
      i.newHotness();
    }
  }' By default, the inspection doesn't produce a warning if it's impossible or hard to avoid it. For example, the following code won't be reported: 'abstract class A { //library code
     @Deprecated
     abstract void m();
  }
  class B extends A { //project code
     @Override
     void m() {
        //doSmth;
     }
  }' Configure the inspection: Use the options to disable this inspection inside deprecated members, overrides of abstract deprecated methods, non-static import statements, methods of deprecated classes, or same top-level classes. Inspection ID: Deprecation

