fullDescription.text:
Reports methods that override a super method without calling it. This is also known as a refused bequest. Such methods may represent a failure of abstraction and cause hard-to-trace bugs. The inspection doesn't report methods overridden from 'java.lang.Object', except for 'clone()'. The 'clone()' method should by convention call its super method, which will return an object of the correct type. Example 1: 'class A {
