Reports classes that may be serialized or deserialized. A class may be serialized if it supports the 'Serializable' interface, and its 'readObject()' and 'writeObject()' methods are not defined to always throw an exception. Serializable classes may be dangerous in code intended for secure use. Example: 'class DeserializableClass implements Serializable { // the class doesn't contain 'writeObject()' method throwing an exception
