Reports instantiations of new 'Long', 'Integer', 'Short', or 'Byte' objects that have a primitive 'long', 'integer', 'short', or 'byte' argument. It is recommended that you use the static method 'valueOf()' introduced in Java 5. By default, this method caches objects for values between -128 and 127 inclusive. Example: 'Integer i = new Integer(1);
