Reports 'return' statements with 'null' return values. While occasionally useful, this construct may make the code more prone to failing with a 'NullPointerException'. If a method is designed to return 'null', it is suggested to mark it with the '@Nullable' annotation - such methods will be ignored by this inspection. Example: 'class Person {
    public String getName () {
