fullDescription.text:
Reports usages of 'instanceof' or 'getClass() == SomeClass.class' in which a 'this' expression is checked. Such expressions indicate a failure of the object-oriented design, and should be replaced by polymorphic constructions. Example: 'class Super {
  void process() {
    if (this instanceof Sub) { // warning
      doSomething();
    } else {
      doSomethingElse();
    }
  }
}

class Sub extends Super {}' To fix the problem, use an overriding method: 'class Super {
  void process() {
    doSomethingElse();
  }
}

class Sub extends Super {
  @Override
  void process() {
    doSomething();
  }
}' Inspection ID: InstanceofThis

fullDescription.markdown:
Reports usages of `instanceof` or `getClass() == SomeClass.class` in which a `this` expression is checked.

Such expressions indicate a failure of the object-oriented design, and should be replaced by
polymorphic constructions.

Example:


    class Super {
      void process() {
        if (this instanceof Sub) { // warning
          doSomething();
        } else {
          doSomethingElse();
        }
      }
    }

    class Sub extends Super {}

To fix the problem, use an overriding method:


    class Super {
      void process() {
        doSomethingElse();
      }
    }

    class Sub extends Super {
