Reports alias expressions that duplicate names of columns in tables and might be redundant. Example (PostgreSQL): 'CREATE TABLE foo(a INT, b INT);

SELECT * FROM foo foo(a, b);
SELECT * FROM foo foo(a);
SELECT * FROM foo foo(x);
SELECT * FROM foo foo(x, y);' The first two aliases use the same column names as in the 'foo' table. They are considered redundant because they column names are identical. Inspection ID: SqlRedundantAliasInspection

