fullDescription.text:
Reports invalid cases of subprogram overloading in Oracle. Example (Oracle): 'DECLARE
    SUBTYPE fff IS BINARY_INTEGER;
    SUBTYPE ggg IS NATURAL;
    PROCEDURE foo (a IN ggg) IS BEGIN NULL; END;
    PROCEDURE foo (a IN fff) IS BEGIN NULL; END;
BEGIN
    NULL;
END;' You cannot overload subprograms which parameters differ only in subtypes. For example, you cannot overload procedures where one accepts a BINARY INTEGER parameter and the other accepts a NATURAL parameter. For more information about restrictions on procedure overloading, see Restrictions on Overloading at docs.oracle.com. Inspection ID: OraOverloadInspection

fullDescription.markdown:
Reports invalid cases of subprogram overloading in Oracle.

